<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n608" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Actē</span></b> , ēs,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀκτή</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>coastland</i> or <i>maritime country;</i> hence, <i>the
				earlier name for Attica</i>, the province of Middle Greece, in
			which Athens was situated, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 7, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 14,
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the Horae</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. F.
			183</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A concubine
				 of Nero</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Ner. 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 13, 12</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 735</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">2885</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
